title: CorporateStart
position: 79,12
---
You're not just another face in the dim, smokey corner of the bar.

Unlike the usual crowd of illicit deal hunters and disillusioned street hustlers, you stand out.

You lean against a wooden pillar, sipping a glass of bourbon.

This isn't your usual haunt.

The crisp lines of your tailored suit and your air of polished confidence scream sophistication, creating a stark contrast with the gritty ambiance of the dive bar.

Yet, tonight, necessity outweighs comfort, which is why you find yourself here, waiting for the mysterious figure.

You've made your mark in the city's financial elite, a world of high-stakes deals and cutthroat competition.

But lately, the thrill is gone.

Fangs & Finances used to be your playground, but now, corporate protocals feel suffocating, and your influence is waning.

So, when you heard whispers of an underground Fixer known for her formidable reputation and discretion.

Who only recruits the best of the best.

You decide to take on the daunting task of robbing one of the most secure banks.

You don't wait long before you spot her walking through the door.

She's a striking figure, radiating an undeniable presence with each purposeful step.

Her confident stride and piercing, discerning gaze seem to take in every inch of the bar's surroundings, searching for threats and opportunities alike.

When her eyes finally land on you, she glides acorss the bustling room with purpose, cutting through the haze of  smoke and whispered conversations.

<<jump FirstFixerDiscussion>>
===

title: FirstFixerDiscussion
position: 79,237
---
Fixer: I take it your are my contact.
Player: Is that so obvious?
Fixer: It looks like you're waiting for someone; it also looks like you'd be too scared to scuff your shoes by walking into a bar like this.
Player: I take it you have a job for me?
-> I want to make sure this stays between us.
    <<jump Choice_1_1>>
-> Listen, I'm willing to get my hands dirty
    <<jump Choice_1_2>>

===

title: Choice_1_1
position: 45,462
---
Fixer: No need to worry; all offers and jobs remain strictly confidential between me and the client.
Fixer: However, what you should be concerned about is whether I'm going to take on the job.
Player: So, you haven't made a decision yet.
Fixer: No, I have made a decision; I just want to make sure it's still the right one.

The Fixer leads you to a nearby seat, the dim light casting shadows across the room, as you continue your discussion.

Fixer: Why this job at your bank, out of all the banks in this city.
Player: We have a high-value client who just transferred their safe and money to our bank.
Player: Of all the safes we have, this is the most valuable one.
Player: If we can retrieve the money, we'll be set for life.
Player: Even if we manage to access some of the other safes, there's a solid chance we'll never have to worry about money again.
Fixer: Why take the risk?
Player: I'm tired of working hard for money, spending time networking with the elite who rarely acknowledge me because I don't have their wealth.
-> Will you take the job?
    <<jump Choice_2_1>>
-> When we do this job, what's the plan?
    <<jump Choice_2_2>>
===

title: Choice_1_2
position: 325,462
---
Fixer: Oh you will.
Player: What's the plan?
Player: When are we going to do this?
Player: Who's on the crew?
Fixer: Relax, I've orchestrated every detail.
Fixer: We kick things off in a week.
Fixer: I've brought together a skilled team of four, each of them trusthworthy and reliable.
Fixer: That's all you need to know for the moment.
===

